"_note": [
"The house look for photographs, as a lookup table: for each possible value",
"of red, green and blue from 0 to 255, the value it becomes.",
"",
"It was not invented here. The thirteen colour photographs already on the",
"site were graded by hand, and this table was measured back off them by",
"comparing each finished photograph against its original, so that anything",
"uploaded later is treated identically rather than approximately. Replayed",
"against those originals it reproduces the finished versions to within 2.2",
"levels out of 255 \u2014 under one per cent.",
"",
"What it does: an S-curve that deepens the shadows and opens the highlights,",
"split-toned cool in the dark parts and warm in the light ones. That is what",
"makes a phone snapshot and a camera frame look like one body of work.",
"",
"The black-and-white portrait was excluded from the measurement: it has its",
"own treatment and would have polluted the average."
